---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/service.css";

const SITE = "https://www.tmdesignengineering.com";
const url = `${SITE}/for-startups`;
const jsonld = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebPage",
    "@id": `${url}#page`,
    url,
    name: "For Startups, senior design engineering without the full-time hire",
    isPartOf: { "@id": `${SITE}/#website` },
    about: { "@id": `${SITE}/#business` },
    description:
      "Senior design engineering for hardware startups: momentum on the roadmap, verification and manufacturing preparation, and a product carried toward production.",
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    itemListElement: [
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${SITE}/` },
      { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "For Startups", item: url },
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="For Startups, Senior Design Engineering On Demand | Thomas McKee"
  description="Engineering muscle for hardware startups without a full-time hire. Keep the roadmap moving, verify a design before tooling, and prepare it for volume manufacture, from an engineer who has shipped to mass production."
  type="website"
  jsonld={jsonld}>
<main>
  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="svc-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow">For startups</span>
      <h1>Engineering muscle, <em>without the full-time hire</em></h1>
      <p class="lede">Maybe you're moving fast on a product, but a senior hardware engineer is a big, early commitment. I give startups that experience on demand: momentum on the roadmap, the hard problems solved, and a product carried toward production. All from someone who has actually shipped consumer hardware to mass manufacture.</p>
      <div class="svc-hero-cta">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/services/product-development">See how it works</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PAIN -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">If this sounds like you</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Where startups get stuck</h2>
      <div class="pain">
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"We need senior engineering, but can't justify a full-time hire yet."</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"We have a design, but is it actually ready to verify and manufacture?"</p></div>
        <div class="q"><span class="mk">?</span><p>"How do we keep momentum without making an expensive mistake?"</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="sec-intro">What I offer is speed with a structured process: experienced engineering that keeps the roadmap moving and heads off the costly mistakes before they're baked into tooling. You get the reach of a senior hire, scoped to exactly what you need right now.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW I HELP -->
  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">How I plug in</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">A technical partner, scoped to your specific needs</h2>
      <p class="sec-intro">Bring me in for the whole journey, or for the specific stage you're at right now. Most startups already have a design in motion, so verification and manufacturing prep are common entry points.</p>
      <div class="aud-grid">
        <a class="aud" href="/services/product-development">
          <div class="aud-top"><h3>Product Development</h3><span class="aud-tag">Partnership</span></div>
          <p>The full managed journey in scoped, gated phases, with a network of specialists brought in as the product needs them.</p>
          <span class="aud-go">Product Development <span class="arw">→</span></span>
        </a>
        <a class="aud" href="/services/design-verification">
          <div class="aud-top"><h3>Design Verification</h3></div>
          <p>Prove the design performs, is safe and is compliant before you commit to tooling, with analysis, simulation and structured testing. Catch expensive compliance or performance issues while they're cheap to solve.</p>
          <span class="aud-go">Design Verification <span class="arw">→</span></span>
        </a>
        <a class="aud" href="/services/manufacturing-preparation">
          <div class="aud-top"><h3>Manufacturing Preparation</h3></div>
          <p>Get a proven design ready for efficient volume manufacture: DFMA, production CAD, a drawing pack with GD&amp;T, and liaison with your chosen factory in the UK or overseas.</p>
          <span class="aud-go">Manufacturing Preparation <span class="arw">→</span></span>
        </a>
        <a class="aud" href="/services/contract-engineering">
          <div class="aud-top"><h3>Contract Engineering</h3></div>
          <p>Retained or day-rate capacity when you just need a safe pair of senior hands on a defined brief, remote or on-site, slotting into how your team already works.</p>
          <span class="aud-go">Contract Engineering <span class="arw">→</span></span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHY ME -->
  <section class="band alt">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="sec-idx">Why startups work with me</span>
      <h2 class="sec-title">Proven experience making products that have shipped at volume</h2>
      <div class="proof">
        <div class="pl">The difference</div>
        <p>The biggest oversight most startups make is not knowing the difference between a design that works and a product that ships economically at scale. I've been at both stages, having taken consumer products from concept through to volume manufacture, and been in the drawing room and on the factory floor. That means the decisions I make early are made by someone who has seen how they play out in production, so momentum now doesn't mean racing ahead with risks that might cause you a redesign later.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="svc-cred">
        <span class="ci"><b>Mechanical, firmware, thermal &amp; manufacture</b> as one system</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Shipped to medium and high volume</b>, UK &amp; overseas</span>
        <span class="ci"><b>Red Dot &amp; iF award-winning</b> products, patent-protected work</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="band" id="start">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="cta">
        <div class="inner">
          <span class="eyebrow">Let's talk</span>
          <h2 style="margin-top:14px">Need to keep your product moving?</h2>
          <p>Book a free intro call and tell me where the product is and where it's stuck. I'll tell you honestly how I can help and what the right engagement looks like.</p>
          <div class="row">
            <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href="/#contact">Book a free intro call <span class="arw">→</span></a>
            <span class="price-tag">Day rate · retainer · phased</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
<style>
  .aud-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px;margin-top:26px}
  @media(max-width:760px){.aud-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  .aud{display:flex;flex-direction:column;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:14px;background:var(--surface);padding:24px 26px;text-decoration:none;transition:.15s}
  .aud:hover{border-color:var(--ink-3);transform:translateY(-2px)}
  .aud-top{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:12px}
  .aud h3{font-size:1.18rem;letter-spacing:-0.015em;color:var(--ink)}
  .aud p{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:0.98rem;margin-top:10px;line-height:1.5;flex:1}
  .aud-tag{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:10px;letter-spacing:0.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ember);border:1px solid var(--ember);border-radius:20px;padding:2px 9px;flex:none}
  .aud-go{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;margin-top:18px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:12.5px;color:var(--ember)}
</style>
</Base>
